; What the Lojix Nexus sends into the world: every external call a deploy or
; test pipeline makes, each one emission, and the outcome its translator
; observed. A command line is a type: an emission names what is asked, a
; field per argument, and the translator, in src/translator.rs, is the one
; place that holds the words of the call, a process's program and argv or a
; systemd D-Bus method. A path or a name Lojix forms is its own newtype over
; a String; a bare String stands only for text the world wrote, what a
; process printed or a fault reported. A unit's ActiveState and its service
; Result are systemd's documented values, each with the value systemd may
; add later kept as the text it sent.
;
; Whether the running boot loader implements the EFI boot loader interface
; is read on the node before its boot entries are cleared, the check bootctl
; itself makes: the LoaderInfo variable the loader sets at boot. A loader
; that does not implement it has no entries of this interface to clear, so
; a host switched under it is never asked to clear them, and a self-switch
; script carries no clears.
;
; The process emissions run under the effect execution, which says where a
; program comes from; the D-Bus emissions run on one system-bus session that
; keeps the subscriptions a detached activation is watched through. An
; attempt, one stage of a pipeline, composes the emissions it needs; each
; emission is emitted on a blocking thread and awaited.
Emission

[ signal_lojix:[ FlakeReference DeploymentOutputSelector ClosurePath NixStoreUri SshDestination
                 NixBuilderSpec NodeName GenerationIdentifier CommandProgram CommandArgument
                 UserName ]
  meta_signal_lojix:[ ExtraSubstituter ]
  :crate:memory:[ PersistedFlakeInputOverride ResolvedRevision ] ]

